#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# exp

#% text
# `exp(x)` gives the exponential function of `x`, `e` to the power `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Exact values: `exp(0)` is 1, `exp(1)` is `e`, `exp(log(y))` is `y`, and `exp(q*pi*im)` for a rational `q` is a root of unity in closed form when `cos` and `sin` of `q*pi` are known exactly.

#% item
# Other exact arguments stay unevaluated: `exp(2)` is kept as it is. Use `n` for a numerical value.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% item
# `exp` is listable: it applies to each element of a list.

#% item
# Products of exponentials are not combined automatically: `exp(x)*exp(y)` stays as it is.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
exp(0)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
exp(1)
#% output
#= e

#% text
# A machine number:

#% cell
exp(2.0)
#% output
#= 7.38905609893065

#% text
# The exponential undoes the logarithm:

#% cell
exp(log(5))
#% output
#= 5

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Imaginary multiples of `pi` give exact values:

#% cell
exp(pi*im)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
exp(pi*im/3)
#% output
#= 1/2 + (im/2)*3^(1/2)

#% text
# A ball, and 30 digits from an exact argument:

#% cell
exp(1~30)
#% output
#= 2.71828182845904523536028747135

#% cell
n(exp(1), 30)
#% output
#= 2.7182818284590452353602874713526625

#% text
# A complex machine number:

#% cell
exp(1.0 + 2.0*im)
#% output
#= -1.1312043837568135 + 2.4717266720048188im

#% text
# Each element of a list:

#% cell
exp([0, 1, log(2)])
#% output
#= [1, e, 2]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `exp` is its own derivative, up to the chain rule:

#% cell
d(exp(3x), x)
#% output
#= 3*exp(3*x)

#% text
# The power series:

#% cell
series(exp(x), x, 0, 5)
#% output
#= 1 + x + x^2/2 + x^3/6 + x^4/24 + x^5/120 + O(x^6)

#% text
# `exp(x)` and `e^x` agree to any number of digits:

#% cell
n(exp(2), 30)
#% output
#= 7.389056098930650227230427460575008

#% cell
n(e^2, 30)
#% output
#= 7.389056098930650227230427460575008

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# Large machine arguments overflow to infinity; use an exact argument and `n` with digits instead:

#% cell
exp(1000.0)
#% output
#= inf

#% cell
n(exp(1000), 20)
#% output
#= 1.970071114017046993889e434

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `log`, `sin`, `cos`, `exp_to_trig`, `sqrt`, `n`
